### Problem or use case

The current Open With implementation from [#421](https://github.com/lgse/strata/pull/421), with follow-ups in [#578](https://github.com/lgse/strata/pull/578), provides the chooser for selected files.

However, some useful behaviors are still missing:

- recommended and other applications are not shown in separate sections;
- users cannot browse all other visible applications;
- there is no search field for finding applications quickly;
- the folder background context menu does not provide an “Open With…” action when right-clicking empty space.

### Proposed solution

Improve the Open With chooser and folder context menu by:

- showing recommended applications using `AppInfo::all_for_type()`;
- showing other visible applications using `AppInfo::all()`;
- filtering hidden applications;
- removing duplicate applications between both sections;
- adding a search field that filters applications while typing;
- keeping the “Recommended Apps” and “Other Apps” sections visible when applicable;
- showing an appropriate empty state when the search has no matches;
- adding an “Open With…” action to the folder background context menu;
- using the current directory as the target for that action;
- adding tests for application grouping, search, and the folder background context menu.

### Search behavior

The search should:

- be focused when the chooser opens;
- filter applications from both sections;
- be case-insensitive;
- update results as the user types;
- preserve keyboard navigation;
- allow the search to be cleared easily.

### Alternatives considered

- Keep the chooser limited to recommended applications.
- Show all applications in a single list.
- Require users to scroll through the full application list instead of providing search.

